Let G = (V, E) be a finite simple planar graph with maximum degree Δ(G). The square of G, denoted G², is the graph on the same vertex set V in which two distinct vertices u, v are adjacent if and only if their distance in G is at most 2. Let χ(G²) denote the chromatic number of G².

Prove or disprove the following (Wegner's planar graph conjecture): for every planar graph G,
  χ(G²) ≤ 7, if Δ(G) = 3;
  χ(G²) ≤ Δ(G) + 5, if 4 ≤ Δ(G) ≤ 7;
  χ(G²) ≤ ⌊3Δ(G)/2⌋ + 1, if Δ(G) ≥ 8.

In particular, establish the bound χ(G²) ≤ ⌊3Δ(G)/2⌋ + 1 for all planar graphs G with Δ(G) ≥ 8, and the sharp small-degree bounds stated above.

